{
  "matched": [
    {
      "goldenId": "GV3-001",
      "findingId": "SP-002",
      "note": "Same root cause as GV3-001: CheckPolicy's `if baseErr != nil { if policy.Mode == PolicyModeFree { return nil, nil } ... }` guard (policy.go:329-336) checks policy.Mode from the pre-basePolicy, attacker-editable working-tree Policy struct passed into CheckPolicy — before the trusted base-branch policy is ever loaded (basePolicy() is only called after this branch, line 337). An attacker who sets working-tree policy.Mode=\"free\" and causes policyBase to fail (e.g. an unreachable/forged base_ref) hits this untrusted free-mode short-circuit instead of the hard error. Same 'working base_ref -> pre-policy base -> free-mode short-circuit disables gate' mechanism GV3-001 names; SP-002 just narrates the attack via the resolution-failure branch."
    }
  ],
